{"kind":"request","text":"Root pages carry docset front matter that no gate reads.\n\nSKILL.md carries a `rests_on` list of behaviour citations and maintains it by\nhand, but `internal/docset/docset.go:20` sets `DocsDir = \"docs\"`, so none of\nthe documentation gates ever reads it. That is how seven of its twelve\ncitations came to be retired without any gate noticing; the defect was found\nonly because `gs artifact` refused a publication that rested on them\n(landed at 02090dc2, verdict 7d3ef0e5).\n\nEither bring the root pages into the gate's scope, or stop maintaining\nunguarded front matter by hand. Decide which; both are defensible, and the\npresent state is not.","body":{"conditions":"1. A decision is recorded either way: root pages in scope, or root pages without rests_on front matter.\n2. If in scope: the gate reads SKILL.md (and any other root page carrying rests_on) and fails or reports on a dead citation exactly as it does for a page under docs/, with a test that goes red when a cited artifact is retired.\n3. If out of scope: the hand-maintained front matter is removed from the root pages, and the behaviour citations live somewhere a gate does read, or the page says plainly that it carries none.\n4. `make docs` and `make test` green at the exact head.","target_head":"02090dc2df7d06f05c8fb9b6be54b857c883a8cb","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}